#%PAM-1.0
# GDM's fingerprint service, which the login and lock screens offer beside the password once a
# finger is enrolled (Settings, Users): fprintd's PAM module, and nothing else that would ask for a
# password. The login keyring has no password of its own (construct clearKeyring), so it opens the
# same after a finger as after the password. GDM's own build ships no such file for Wolfi's stack.
auth       requisite   pam_nologin.so
auth       required    pam_fprintd.so
-auth      optional    pam_gnome_keyring.so
account    include     base-account
password   required    pam_deny.so
session    include     base-session
-session   optional    pam_gnome_keyring.so auto_start
